{
  "changelog": "Initial release of the \"method-cohesion-diagnostic\" skill for psychology academic writing.\n\n- Diagnoses cohesion and coherence issues in the Method section of psychology papers, focusing on sequence accuracy, paragraph transitions, inter-module logic, and referential clarity.\n- Applies comprehensive criteria from *Science Research Writing* (2nd ed.), Unit 2 \u00a72.4.2 and the Generic Methods Model.\n- Utilizes a 117-item checklist, detailed scoring rubric (A/B/C/D/F), and top-tier journal exemplars as diagnostic references.\n- Outputs clear scores and provides specific examples of best practices for sequence language, transitions, logical flow, and reference usage.\n- Designed for integration with related diagnostics on structure, logic, grammar, and vocabulary.",
